spans.s:
लोक॑ m. open space^1, free room, place, region,
[]
world
or one of the (imaginary 2, 3, or 7) worlds, esp. the earth;
 people, men
or mankind (sgl. or pl.);
 company, community, troop or band of (—˚);
worldy life, ordinary practice or common usage (opp. to higher things,
esp. knowledge).
[1] Correction submitted by AnnaRybakovaT, Jim Funderburk. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/25.

लोकनाथ m. lord of the worlds (Brahman, Viṣṇu, or
Śiva);
 also ruler of men, king.

लोकयात्रा f. business and traffic of men;
 support of
life, daily bread.

लोकसाक्षिक a. witnessed by the world or by men;
 n.
adv.

लोकि॑न् a. possessing the (best) world;
 pl. the inhabitants
of the universe.

लोक्य॑ a. granting free space or sphere of action;
world-wide, usual, customary right;
 real, actual. — n. free space or
sphere.
